2026-10-13: executed-instruction attribution for K02, K03, K10, K11f and K01b.
Diagnostic only. No kernel, Image, contract, timeout or verdict changes.
K02, K03, K10, K11f and K01b stay OPEN.

Retention gap. The pinned 7,008-object pair (EvoCC 18b36fee, GCC 22a87df2,
config 95853321) was deleted with .build/k7-coverage on October 7, with its
payloads and BPF/BTF inputs. This profile uses the retained direct
virtconfig pair from the same pinned source and input config:
  GCC   .build/reference/gcc-lane-1        Image b6f206de  config 4245f8e6
  EvoCC .build/case/kbuild-probe/out-k16   Image add1c487  config 14679920
        (K16/K17 build, compiler 820bfa29; olddefconfig capability changes)
Both sign returns. EvoCC signs every function, GCC only non-leaf ones.
These numbers are not results for the 7,008-object composition.

Lane. The QEMU argv of tools/k1/lib.sh k1_boot on tcg-neoverse-n2-el2
(virt-11.0, EL2, GICv3, 4 vCPUs, 4 GiB), plus two diagnostic changes: the
tbprof plugin and `nokaslr`. QEMU is Homebrew 11.1.2 (2239f9f1), an
explicit drift from the contract's 11.0.3 (af7f6f87). Host load average was
26-90 from other jobs, so all wall-clock values are load-bound.

Method. tools/k1/perf/tbprof.c (QEMU plugin API 7) counts entries of each
translation block per vCPU with an inline add and keeps its code words;
instructions = entries x block length. A block that faults counts in full.
Marker PCs write snapshots: kvm_arch_init_vm/kvm_arch_destroy_vm bound one
guest VM; __arm64_sys_unshare/__arm64_sys_reboot bound the pidfd loop;
__arm64_sys_arm64_personality brackets the BPF proxy. attribute.py maps each
instruction to its vmlinux FUNC symbol. With --right-inline, GCC code goes to
the innermost DWARF inline frame that EvoCC also ran as a function, so an
inlined GCC helper is compared with EvoCC's out-of-line copy. No block was
dropped or irregular in any run. The first two four-vCPU validation boots
per Image used an earlier build without discon=off (cc7f4b36); all other
runs used the build below. Plugin build (Apple clang 21.0.0):
  clang -O2 -shared -fPIC -undefined dynamic_lookup -I/opt/homebrew/include \
    $(pkg-config --cflags glib-2.0) -Wall -Wextra -Werror tbprof.c -o tbprof.dylib
Validation, same boot twice on one vCPU: GCC 259,827,973 / 260,105,274
(0.11%), EvoCC 1,197,435,354 / 1,196,509,572 (0.08%); user space 848,436 /
848,422 and 2,002,306 / 2,002,287. Four-vCPU totals vary by up to 27% from
spin loops, so four-vCPU phases are compared only for equal work.
QEMU 11.1.2 aborts at start (arm_mmu_idx_el) when a plugin with per-vCPU
inline counters runs under thread=single; an empty plugin does not. -icount
therefore cannot be used (reproducer: qemu-thread-single/inlineonly.c).

